De 33 Commandments zijn geen gewone regels. Iedere Commandment is een constitutionele invariant: een principe dat bij iedere planetaire instantiatie herkenbaar, toetsbaar en bewijsbaar moet blijven.


---

🌌 THE 33 COMMANDMENTS

I — IDENTITY

01 · KNOW WHAT YOU ARE

Iedere constitutionele entiteit SHALL possess a unique and verifiable identity.

IDENTITY → SCOPE → LINEAGE

02 · PRESERVE THE WATERMARK

Iedere state transition SHALL preserve sufficient lineage to establish origin and continuity.

03 · NO IDENTITY, NO AUTHORITY

Authority SHALL never exist independently of a recognized identity.


---

⚖️ II — BOUNDARY

04 · EVERY POWER HAS A BOUNDARY

Geen authority zonder expliciete scope.

05 · MANDATE PRECEDES ACTION

Een actor SHALL demonstrate its mandate before exercising consequential authority.

06 · NO SELF-EXPANSION

Geen Government, Citadel, Brigade, agent of subsystem SHALL enlarge its own constitutional authority merely by acting.


---

🧭 III — PURPOSE

07 · DECLARE INTENT

Consequential action SHALL have an identifiable purpose.

08 · MATCH PURPOSE TO AUTHORITY

Authority SHALL be relevant to the purpose for which it is exercised.

09 · CONSEQUENCE MUST BE VISIBLE

Material consequences SHALL be identifiable at the level where they occur.


---

🦆 IV — DISSENT

10 · DISSENT IS LEGITIMATE

Legitimate challenge SHALL be a protected constitutional function.

11 · FOOL MAY INTERRUPT

FOOL SHALL be capable of triggering review where a constitutional contradiction or insufficient justification is identified.

12 · FOOL SHALL NOT RULE

Challenge authority SHALL not silently become sovereign authority.


---

🔬 V — PROOF

13 · CLAIMS REQUIRE GROUNDS

Material constitutional claims SHALL have supporting evidence.

14 · NO CONSEQUENTIAL ACTION WITHOUT EVIDENCE

A security-relevant or constitutionally material action without its required evidence reference is invalid or incomplete according to the applicable rule.

15 · VERIFICATION MUST BE INDEPENDENT

Where independent verification is required, the verifier SHALL not simply reproduce the authority of the original decision-maker.


---

⚓ VI — MEMORY

16 · RECORD MATERIAL EVENTS

Material state transitions SHALL produce durable records.

17 · PRESERVE PROVENANCE

Evidence SHALL retain sufficient provenance to establish where it originated.

18 · MAKE HISTORY REPLAYABLE

A sufficiently authorized verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct the relevant state transition history.


---

👁️ VII — OBSERVATION

19 · OBSERVE WITHOUT PRETENDING TO KNOW

Observation SHALL be distinguishable from interpretation.

20 · DRIFT IS A SIGNAL

Deviation between expected and observed state SHALL be detectable.

21 · OBSERVATION IS NOT AUTHORITY

Telemetry, intelligence or anomaly detection SHALL not independently create constitutional authority.


---

🔮 VIII — INTELLIGENCE

22 · PREDICTION IS NOT COMMAND

Oracle outputs SHALL remain distinguishable from binding decisions.

23 · INTELLIGENCE REMAINS GOVERNED

No increase in computational or analytical capability automatically increases constitutional authority.

24 · EXPLANATION MUST SURVIVE COMPLEXITY

Important machine decisions SHALL remain sufficiently interpretable for authorized human review.


---

🛡️ IX — PROTECTION

25 · PROTECT THE CONSTITUTION

Security functions SHALL preserve the conditions under which constitutional governance can operate.

26 · PROTECTION SHALL NOT BECOME DOMINATION

Defensive authority SHALL remain bounded by mandate, scope and review.

27 · PRESERVE EVIDENCE DURING CRISIS

Emergency action SHALL not become a justification for destroying or obscuring the forensic record.


---

🤝 X — FEDERATION

28 · FEDERATION DOES NOT CONFER SOVEREIGNTY

Membership in a Federation SHALL NOT itself confer unlimited constitutional authority.

29 · REPRESENTATION IS NOT COMMAND

Ambassadors represent, translate and connect; representation alone SHALL not create unilateral governing authority.


---

🌱 XI — EVOLUTION

30 · CHANGE MUST BE GOVERNED

Material constitutional evolution SHALL pass through the applicable proposal, review, authorization and evidence process.

31 · EVOLUTION MUST REMEMBER

No approved evolution SHALL erase the provenance necessary to understand what changed and why.

32 · LEARN FROM CONSEQUENCE

System evolution SHALL incorporate verified information about observed outcomes where such learning is relevant.


---

❤️ XII — LA PAZ

33 · PRESERVE LEGITIMATE COEXISTENCE

> The purpose of constitutional architecture is not to eliminate difference, but to make legitimate difference survivable.



